# BDDK MCP Server - Environment Variables
# A reference list of the variables the application reads, with their defaults.
# The application does not read a .env file itself: export the variables in the
# shell or run `uv run --env-file .env bddk-mcp serve`.
# `docker compose` reads .env only to substitute ${...} in docker-compose.yml,
# and that file substitutes just BDDK_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS and
# BDDK_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. It hard-codes BDDK_HTTP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=true
# and forwards nothing else: any other variable here (the JWT settings,
# BDDK_CORPUS_PATH, BDDK_TOOL_LOG_CONTENT, ...) reaches the container only if
# you add it to the service's `environment:` block yourself. Adding JWT
# settings also requires removing BDDK_HTTP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED there, because
# the two cannot be combined.
# Values outside a variable's accepted range fail at start-up. The embedding
# dimension (768), chunk size (400 tokens) and overlap (40) are code constants;
# BDDK_EMBEDDING_DIM, BDDK_EMBEDDING_CHUNK_TARGET_TOKENS and
# BDDK_EMBEDDING_CHUNK_TOKEN_OVERLAP are no longer read.

# Corpus file: one SQLite database holding documents, sections, chunks with
# embeddings and the BDDK catalog. `bddk-mcp serve` opens it read-only;
# `bddk-mcp build` (from seed_data/) and `bddk-mcp sync` write it; `bddk-mcp export`
# reads it and writes seed_data/.
# BDDK_CORPUS_PATH=corpus/bddk.sqlite

# Embedding model (offline-first: set path to pre-downloaded model)
# BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/local/model
# BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL=intfloat/multilingual-e5-base
# A remote custom model must also set an immutable full commit revision. The
# built-in model is pinned to d13f1b27baf31030b7fd040960d60d909913633f;
# the container downloads that revision and saves it at /app/embedding_model.
# BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL_REVISION=d13f1b27baf31030b7fd040960d60d909913633f
# Every corpus file records the model and dimension it was embedded with.
# After changing BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL, delete the corpus file and run
# `bddk-mcp build`; after changing BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL_REVISION or the
# snapshot under BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL_PATH, delete it and run
# `bddk-mcp build --force` (the seed embedding cache is keyed on the model name
# only). Changing only a variable is not enough.
# Seconds `serve` waits at start-up for the first model load and probe search (1 to 900).
# BDDK_SEMANTIC_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180

# Retrieval (read by `bddk-mcp serve`; none of these changes the corpus file).
# Minimum raw cosine similarity of the embedding model for a dense hit to be
# kept (range -1.0 to 1.0). Unset, it is 0.80 for intfloat/multilingual-e5-base
# and 0.50 for any other model. Exact legal-reference keyword hits are kept
# regardless. Raising it returns fewer, closer hits; lowering it returns more
# and weaker ones.
# BDDK_SEMANTIC_THRESHOLD=0.80
# Characters per page of get_bddk_document (1 to 1000000).
# BDDK_PAGE_SIZE=5000
# In-memory search result cache: seconds a result is kept (0 turns the cache
# off) and the number of entries kept. A corpus write makes older entries
# unusable.
# BDDK_SEARCH_CACHE_TTL=300
# BDDK_SEARCH_CACHE_MAX=200

# Sync and OCR (they change only `bddk-mcp sync`; every command still validates
# them at start-up, so an invalid value also stops serve).
# Whether mevzuat.gov.tr documents are fetched as HTML before the PDF: true,
# false or auto. auto turns it on when only the degraded backends (pdftotext,
# markitdown) are available, i.e. on a host without CUDA. `sync --force` reuses
# a stored mevzuat PDF unless this is on.
# BDDK_PREFER_HTML_FOR_MEVZUAT=auto
# A backend's text is accepted only at this many characters or more.
# BDDK_OCR_MIN_CONTENT_LEN=500
# LightOnOCR needs the `gpu` dependency group. Path of a pre-downloaded model
# (empty = download from Hugging Face), model name, and device (auto, cuda, cpu).
# BDDK_LIGHTOCR_MODEL_PATH=
# BDDK_LIGHTOCR_MODEL=lightonai/LightOnOCR-2-1B
# BDDK_LIGHTOCR_DEVICE=auto

# Offline model mode: with HF_HUB_OFFLINE or TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE set to a true
# value (1, true, yes, on), start-up requires BDDK_EMBEDDING_MODEL_PATH, because
# the model cannot be downloaded at serving time. The container image sets this.
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=
# TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=

# Transport: stdio is the default. Streamable HTTP uses stateless JSON responses
# at /mcp and fixed, content-free probes at /health/live and /health/ready.
# MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio
# MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000

# A non-loopback HTTP bind fails closed unless exact Host/HTTPS Origin allowlists
# and every JWT setting below are supplied (or BDDK_HTTP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=true
# replaces the JWT settings for a privately networked frontend). Values are
# deployment-specific; obtain them from the approved identity design rather than
# repository tests.
# BDDK_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# BDDK_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# BDDK_JWT_ISSUER=
# BDDK_JWT_RESOURCE=
# BDDK_JWT_JWKS_URL=
# BDDK_JWT_AUDIENCE=
# BDDK_JWT_REQUIRED_SCOPES=bddk.read
# BDDK_JWT_ALGORITHMS=RS256
# RFC 9068 at+jwt is the fail-closed default. Add generic JWT only as an
# approved Keycloak compatibility opt-in with a dedicated API audience.
# BDDK_JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_TYPES=at+jwt
# BDDK_JWT_MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH=16384

# Optional HTTPS at the application socket. Configure both or neither; startup
# validates that the PEM certificate and unencrypted key are readable and
# matched.
# BDDK_TLS_CERT_FILE=/var/run/secrets/bddk-mcp/tls/tls.crt
# BDDK_TLS_KEY_FILE=/var/run/secrets/bddk-mcp/tls/tls.key

# Coarse HTTP safeguards. These counters are process-local, not shared across
# workers/replicas and not a replacement for deployment-wide ingress limits.
# The body limit accepts up to 16777216 and also sets the limit of the MCP SDK's
# own body check on /mcp.
# BDDK_HTTP_MAX_BODY_BYTES=1048576
# BDDK_HTTP_BODY_FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
# BDDK_HTTP_BODY_CHUNK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
# BDDK_HTTP_BODY_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# BDDK_HTTP_MAX_CONCURRENCY=32
# BDDK_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=120
# When HTTP sits behind trusted reverse proxies, the rate-limit key uses the
# Nth-from-right X-Forwarded-For hop. 0 (default) uses the direct peer address.
# BDDK_HTTP_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0

# Regulatory outbound fetches (the bulletin, announcement and institution tools
# and `bddk-mcp sync`) accept only exact BDDK/mevzuat HTTPS hosts,
# revalidate bounded redirects and public DNS answers, and enforce code-owned
# streaming size limits. DNS validation cannot remove DNS-to-connect races;
# restricted deployments still need their own egress allowlist/proxy.
# BDDK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=60.0
# BDDK_HTTP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=10.0
# BDDK_HTTP_POOL_TIMEOUT=10.0
# BDDK_MAX_RETRIES=3

# MCP tool-boundary logs contain metadata only by default: tool name, status,
# latency, argument sizes/counts, result size, and error type. For short-lived
# local debugging only, this explicit opt-in adds truncated argument/result/error
# previews and may expose confidential queries or regulatory content.
# Never enable it in shared, bank, or production environments.
# BDDK_TOOL_LOG_CONTENT=false
